==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|unbinden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|unbindan}}, {{m|ang|onbindan|t=to unbind; untie}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*andabindan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*andabindaną}}, equivalent to {{pre|en|un|id1=reversive|bind}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|ontbinden}}, {{cog|de|entbinden}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌽𐌳𐌱𐌹𐌽𐌳𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌnˈbaɪnd/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unbind.wav|a=Southern England}}
*: {{rhymes|en|aɪnd|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|unbinds|unbinding|unbound|past_ptc2=unbounden|past_ptc2_qual=rare}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[take off|take]] [[binding]]s off.
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To set [[free]] from a [[debt]], [[contract]] or [[promise]].
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive}} To [[disable]] some kind of [[connection]] in [[software]], such as a [[key binding]]. <!--also e.g. in programming-->
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Douglas Chick|title=Minecraft Secrets Book Cheat Codes|page=23
|passage='''Unbinds''' the specified key from a command}}

